Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 1 useful find

Only one genuinely incremental finding cleared the threshold this run.
Previously ingested Higgsfield API, P-Video-2-Pro, Vidu S2, Qwen3.8-Omni,
bg0, Nari Qwen3-TTS, VibeAvatar and HiDream-O1-Video were suppressed as
duplicates.
H3 Max Turbo on fal =E2=80=94 TEST NOW

Source: https://fal.ai/models/minimax/h3-max-turbo/image-to-video
Release/update context: fal=E2=80=99s H3 Max family launched Aug 26; Turbo =
is now
available as a production image-to-video endpoint and was benchmarked in
fal=E2=80=99s Sep 9 speed comparison. This is newly relevant because the pr=
oduction
endpoint exposes exactly the fast, cheap audiovisual path Roast.pet needs.

What changed: H3 Max Turbo is fal=E2=80=99s post-trained MiniMax H3 speed t=
ier. fal
reports 768p generation at $0.04/output-second, with a 5-second render
around 1.4=E2=80=931.5 seconds in current benchmark material. It supports
image-to-video and native synchronized stereo audio/lip movement. The
tradeoff versus full H3 Max is loss of reference-to-video/multi-reference
consistency.

Capability: canonical Roast.pet card -> short audiovisual talking-pet clip,
potentially faster than real time. Inputs/outputs: image + prompt -> 768p
audiovisual video. API/install: fal endpoint
minimax/h3-max-turbo/image-to-video. Pricing: $0.04/output-second at 768p;
roughly $0.20 for 5 seconds or $0.40 for 10 seconds. Commercial use: fal
endpoint marks Commercial use. Privacy/self-hosting: cloud endpoint; do not
assume self-hostability of fal=E2=80=99s post-trained Turbo variant.
Quality/latency: exceptional latency, but lack of reference-to-video is the
key identity-consistency risk for pets.

Exact Roast.pet use case: use Turbo for rapid draft generations and
customer previews; only escalate failed identity/mouth/comedy renders to
full H3 Max/P-Video/another reference-capable model.

Smallest prototype: 20 canonical pet cards x one 5-second roast. Generate
Turbo and full H3 Max side by side. Score identity preservation, mouth
plausibility, joke timing, generation wall time and regeneration rate. If
Turbo passes >=3D80% of cards without escalation, make it the default draft
tier.

Decision: TEST NOW.
TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. H3 Max Turbo as cheap/faster-than-real-time draft animation tier.
   2. bg0 browser-side pet cutout.
   3. Nari/Qwen3-TTS cheap multi-take voice generation.
   4. Higgsfield/fal-style provider abstraction rather than direct model
   coupling.
   5. Automated source-pet -> canonical-card -> final-video identity/QC
   scoring.

CHEAPEST meaningful capability improvement: bg0 browser segmentation
remains effectively $0 marginal inference.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR: H3 Max Turbo makes a 5-second
native-audio pet-video draft roughly a $0.20 operation with reported
generation faster than playback duration. That changes the UX: Roast.pet
can plausibly generate previews interactively instead of treating video as
a slow fulfillment step.

CONCRETE STACK SIMPLIFICATION: split video into two tiers: Turbo draft ->
automated QC -> escalate only failures to reference-capable premium video.
This is better than sending every order directly through the expensive
highest-quality model.

Sources:

   - fal H3 Max Turbo I2V:
   https://fal.ai/models/minimax/h3-max-turbo/image-to-video
   - fal speed benchmark (Sep 9 2026):
   https://fal.ai/learn/tools/fastest-ai-video-generation-models
   - fal H3 Max launch: https://fal.ai/learn/devs/introducing-h3-max-by-fal

